 A small TypeScript library, with no runtime dependency, of building blocks for our services that store,
 exchange and update JSON: configuration files, API payloads and stored records. It is imported by the
 other projects of the team, so its behaviour must follow the published standards it implements.
+
+## JSON Pointer (RFC 6901)
+
+`resolvePointer(document, pointer)` (exported from `src/index.ts`) returns the value a JSON Pointer
+refers to. The empty pointer is the whole document. It throws an `Error` if the pointer is not valid
+(it must be empty or start with `/`, and `~` may only be followed by `0` or `1`), or if it does not
+resolve: missing member, array index out of bounds, the `-` index, a non-canonical array index
+(`01`, `+1`), or a step into a primitive. Only own members of objects are resolved.
+
+Run the tests with `npm test`.
